Embedded React: clip an Image to its borderRadius.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/scene/er_node_internal.h,
engine/scene/compositor.c, engine/rendering/image_scaler.c and
engine/tests/rendering/test_image.c. Proposed upstream as pull request #323.

Only backgrounds and gradients followed a node's corner radius, so an Image
with borderRadius (a card's cover) kept square corners. An Image node now keeps
its per-corner radii, and while one is set the bitmap is clipped to the same
rounded silhouette a background would fill: rows clear of the corner arcs blit
as one rectangle, rows the arcs cut blit their covered span and fade the
anti-aliased fringe as the gradient mask does. A square image takes the
unmasked paths unchanged. An overflow: hidden rounded parent still clips its
children to its rectangle only.

